{
  "uid": "agent-harness",
  "title": "Agent Harness",
  "description": "Week 3 observability (\u00a78.4): one group per required bullet. Generated by scripts/build_dashboard.py from the frozen metric names; edit that script, not this file.",
  "tags": [
    "harness",
    "week3"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "0 \u00b7 Is anything wrong?",
      "id": 1,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failures by layer",
      "description": "THE panel. Every failure anywhere in a run, attributed to the layer a person should go and look at: model, tool, mcp, policy, memory, subagent, guard or agent. Nine legend entries instead of a wall of error strings, because the first question is never 'what was the exception' but 'is this my agent, my tools, my policy, or the model'. Rising 'agent' with everything else flat is the hardest case and the one no other panel shows: nothing broke and the answers are still wrong.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(harness_errors_total[$__rate_interval])) by (layer)",
          "legendFormat": "{{layer}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Success ratio (1h)",
      "description": "Runs that reached a final answer. Note what this is NOT: it says nothing about whether the answer was right. That is the Task quality row, and the gap between the two numbers is the most interesting thing on this dashboard.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.7
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.9
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(harness_runs_total{status=\"success\"}[1h])) / sum(increase(harness_runs_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Active runs",
      "description": "Runs executing right now, all roles. Returns to zero between tasks; a value that sticks is a hook that did not fire on_run_end.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(harness_active_runs)",
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Runs by outcome",
      "description": "success / error / capped / no_progress. The last two are guards working as designed (ADR-047, ADR-049), kept apart from 'error' on purpose: a dashboard that filed a working safety net under failures would raise a false alarm every time the harness protected a run.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(harness_runs_total[$__rate_interval])) by (status)",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "id": 5,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
