    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Repeated identical calls",
      "description": "'Are agents repeatedly calling the same failing tool?' \u2014 counted by fingerprinting the arguments, so it is visible without recording what was passed. Rises before the no-progress guard fires, which makes it a warning rather than a postmortem, and usually means a tool description or a prompt needs work rather than the tool itself.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(harness_repeated_tool_calls_total[$__rate_interval])) by (tool)",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "id": 26,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 78
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Work per run: iterations and tool calls",
      "description": "'How many tools does an average run invoke?' A mean is the right statistic here because the question is about the typical run; the outlier that called forty shows up in Runs by outcome as capped or no_progress. Plotted beside iterations so the ratio between them is readable: many tool calls per iteration is a model batching its work, and one per iteration with a rising count is a model going round in circles.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(harness_run_tool_calls_sum[$__rate_interval])) by (role) / sum(rate(harness_run_tool_calls_count[$__rate_interval])) by (role)",
          "legendFormat": "{{role}} tool calls (mean)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(harness_run_iterations_sum[$__rate_interval])) by (role) / sum(rate(harness_run_iterations_count[$__rate_interval])) by (role)",
          "legendFormat": "{{role}} iterations (mean)",
          "refId": "B"
